{#
    The sign-in email (Step 10.6), in the style of the design's emails: a
    one-click "Sign in" button, with the 6-digit code underneath as a
    backup. Both work for 10 minutes. Laid out by email/_customer.html.twig
    (the email rules of Step 11.0); an account without a name is greeted
    "Hello,".
#}
{% extends 'email/_customer.html.twig' %}
{% import 'email/_customer.html.twig' as layout %}
{% set firstName = name %}

{% block title %}Sign in to Llunio Studios{% endblock %}
{% block preheader %}Your sign-in link for Llunio Studios. Your code is {{ code }}.{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<p style="{{ body }}">Press the button below to sign in and see your orders.</p>
{{ layout.button(link, 'Sign in') }}
<div style="height:32px;line-height:32px;font-size:1px;">&nbsp;</div>
<p style="{{ label }}">Or enter this code on the sign-in page</p>
<p style="{{ body }}letter-spacing:0.2em;" data-login-code>{{ code }}</p>
<p style="{{ body }}">The button and the code work for 10 minutes. If you didn't ask to sign in, you can ignore this email.</p>
{% endblock %}
